 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "This is my poor heart's life, o'er sixty years,\nThe love I had for thee; it has disappeared\nAs the spring in summer disappears.\nIt was mine to keep the dead spirit,\nNot mine to keep its image; and again\nSays this of me: \"That is thy dream, never,\nAnd thou shalt not see nor hear again\nHow they say 'Oh joy! how glad are many\nWhen man is happy!'\" O yes, again\nThou art gone from me, yet remain\nA strange longing still.  Thou wherefore\nDidst bequeath all these things?  How before",
